    "standardized_narrative": "In 2019, Syndicate 623 experienced a mixed prior year reserve development, resulting in a net strengthening of $11.0 million based on analysis of the gross claims development triangles. This contrasts with the reported net release of $3.7 million in the prior year reserve releases section, which is likely due to the gross vs net reporting difference. The strengthening was primarily driven by adverse development on prior year catastrophe events, notably loss creep from Typhoon Jebi (2018) and Hurricane Maria (2017). However, some lines of business, such as Cyber & executive risk and Political, accident & contingency, experienced releases, while Marine, Property, Reinsurance, and Specialty lines saw strengthening. The syndicate's reserving philosophy includes initial risk margins that can be released as uncertainty reduces.",
